Which graph matches $y=-5^{-x}+3$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=3.5cm, height=4.5cm, title={A}, axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-2, xmax=2, ymin=-5, ymax=8, samples=100, clip=true, xtick=\empty, ytick={2,3}, yticklabels=\empty]
\addplot[thick, blue, <->, domain=-1.2:1.8] {-exp(-x*ln(5))+3};
\addplot[dashed, red, domain=-2:2] {3};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*] coordinates {(0,2)};
\node[anchor=south] at (axis cs:-1.35,3) {$3$};
\node[anchor=east] (Ainterceptlabel) at (axis cs:-0.45,2) {$2$};
\draw[thin, shorten <=2pt, shorten >=2pt] (Ainterceptlabel.east) -- (axis cs:0,2);
\end{axis}
\begin{axis}[at={(3.8cm,0)}, anchor=south west, width=3.5cm, height=4.5cm, title={B}, axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-2, xmax=2, ymin=-5, ymax=8, samples=100, clip=true, xtick=\empty, ytick={2,3}, yticklabels=\empty]
\addplot[thick, blue, <->, domain=-1.8:1.2] {-exp(x*ln(5))+3};
\addplot[dashed, red, domain=-2:2] {3};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*] coordinates {(0,2)};
\node[anchor=south] at (axis cs:-1.35,3) {$3$};
\node[anchor=east] (Binterceptlabel) at (axis cs:-0.45,2) {$2$};
\draw[thin, shorten <=2pt, shorten >=2pt] (Binterceptlabel.east) -- (axis cs:0,2);
\end{axis}
\begin{axis}[at={(7.6cm,0)}, anchor=south west, width=3.5cm, height=4.5cm, title={C}, axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-2, xmax=2, ymin=-5, ymax=8, samples=100, clip=true, xtick=\empty, ytick={3,4}, yticklabels=\empty]
\addplot[thick, blue, <->, domain=-0.9:1.8] {exp(-x*ln(5))+3};
\addplot[dashed, red, domain=-2:2] {3};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*] coordinates {(0,4)};
\node[anchor=south] at (axis cs:-1.35,3) {$3$};
\node[anchor=west] at (axis cs:0.65,4) {$4$};
\end{axis}
\begin{axis}[at={(3.8cm,-6.5cm)}, anchor=south west, width=4.5cm, height=5.5cm, title={D}, axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-2, xmax=2, ymin=-5, ymax=1, samples=100, clip=true, xtick=\empty, ytick={-4,-3}, yticklabels=\empty]
\addplot[thick, blue, <->, domain=-0.3:1.8] {-exp(-x*ln(5))-3};
\addplot[dashed, red, domain=-2:2] {-3};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*] coordinates {(0,-4)};
\node[anchor=south] at (axis cs:-1.35,-3) {$-3$};
\node[anchor=west] at (axis cs:0.65,-4) {$-4$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph shown has horizontal asymptote $y=2$, passes through $(0,3)$, and decreases from left to right.
Which equation matches it?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-3.2, xmax=4.5, ymin=0, ymax=6, samples=120, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick={-2,2,4}, ytick={1,2,3,4,5}]
\addplot[thick, blue, <->, domain=-2:4.5] {exp(-x*ln(2))+2};
\addplot[dashed, red, domain=-3.2:4.5] {2};
\node[below] at (axis cs:3,2) {$y=2$};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*, blue] coordinates {(0,3)};
\node[above right] at (axis cs:0,3) {$(0,3)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
